---
description: Never read or dump real environment secret files; use templates only.
alwaysApply: true
---

## Environment files and secrets

- **Do not** use the Read tool, Grep, or any command that prints contents of `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.production`, or other environment files that hold live credentials, **in this or any project**.
- **Do** use `.env.example`, `.env.sample`, or documented variable names when explaining configuration.
- If you need to verify env wiring, describe what variables the code expects and ask the human to confirm values locally. **Never** ask them to paste secrets into chat.
- If a secret already appeared in conversation history, **do not repeat it**; treat it as compromised and suggest rotation if it was exposed.
